   "note": "Load holding fails during a slow leak at 20 degrees, so the walker is lost either way unless the joints outlast the leak; the models differ in which actuator gives out first. Level 1 ties leg force and centre-of-pressure authority to the same capacity (A3, A4) and tips. Level 2 is reverse-kneed (CL-05): standing on one leg takes about 25 kN m at the knee, so with the adopted 26.5 kN m (DQ-026) the knee gives way as supply falls, before load holding engages at 0.4, and the cockpit sinks, at 1.0 m/s; it still drops with the knee at 62.5 kN m and holds through the run at 94 kN m."
