   "note": "A slow leak at 19.5 degrees with load holding working; level 1 locks at about 2.9 s, but its centre-of-pressure limit (A3) and leg sag (A4) have let its CoM drift to the foot edge, so the locked body tips (A5) at 3.6 s. Level 2 is reverse-kneed (CL-05): standing on one leg takes about 25 kN m at the knee, so with the adopted 26.5 kN m (DQ-026) the knee gives way as supply falls, before load holding engages at 0.4, and the cockpit sinks (hard drop at 1.6 m/s). With the knee at 62.5 kN m or more level 2 locks at 2.9 s and holds: there level 1's assumptions, not the actuators, decide."
